# bi-etl-ejuice — Core Repository Guide

## What this repository is

**bi-etl-ejuice** is QuintoAndar's central data engineering monorepo. It consolidates all batch data pipeline logic for the company — intraday and D-1 cadence — across ~771 Airflow DAGs. The primary Python package is `bietlejuice`.

All pipeline logic lives here: raw ingestion from source databases and APIs, data lake transformations, Data Warehouse models, pre-aggregated metrics, and a semantic query layer called Qube. New pipelines are created by adding files to this repository — not by running ad-hoc scripts or configuring external tools directly.

---

## Technology Stack

| Component | Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Orchestration | Apache Airflow | DAG scheduling and task execution |
| Compute / Runtime | Databricks (DBR 16.4, Delta Lake) | Spark job execution and Delta table storage |
| Serving / Metastore | Trino (Hive-compatible) | SQL query interface for BI tools; enabled per-table with `has_hive_sync: true` |
| Visualization | Apache Superset | Dashboards and ad-hoc SQL exploration |
| Metadata Catalog | DataHub | Column-level lineage; fed from governance YAML `lineage:` fields |
| Data Quality | Great Expectations ("Inmetro") | Row-count and column-level assertions defined in `data_quality/{layer}/{table}.yml` |
| Local dev stack | Astro CLI + Docker | Local Airflow; `make run-local-environment` |
| Staging environment | Forno | Pre-production Airflow + Databricks; mandatory test before merging any new DAG |

