## Governance and CI Enforcement

Every `.sql` file in `queries/{layer}/` must have a matching `.yml` in `metadata/{layer}/` with the same base name. CI fails if the pair is missing or the metadata content is invalid.

Key CI checks and their local equivalents:

| CI step | Local command |
|---|---|
| Validate declaration YAMLs | `make validate-dag-declaration-files dag_name=<name>` |
| Validate metadata content | `make validate-metadata-files-content` |
| Validate SQL/metadata pairing | `make validate-metadata-files-exist` |
| Validate lineage consistency | `make validate-lineage-consistency` |
| Validate cross-layer joins | `make validate-cross-layer-joins` (warning only, exits 0) |
| Lint Python | `make check-style` |
| Run unit tests | `make unit-tests` |

A Forno Airflow run is **mandatory** before merging any new DAG. There is no exception to this rule.

