## ConfigurationService — Environment-Aware Config

Never hardcode environment names (`"prod"`, `"forno"`), S3 bucket paths, secret keys, or database connection strings anywhere in the codebase. All environment-specific values are resolved at runtime through `ConfigurationService`:

```python
from bietlejuice.services.configuration_service import ConfigurationService

config = ConfigurationService(environment="prod")
bucket = config.get_bucket()          # resolves to the correct S3 path
schema = config.get_schema("my_dag")  # resolves to the correct metastore schema
```

In SQL query files, use bracket-substituted template params (resolved by the Spark job at runtime):

```sql
WHERE dt_event >= '{load_start_date}'
  AND dt_event < '{load_end_date}'
```

Never mix bracket params (`{load_start_date}`) with Jinja expressions (`{{ ds }}`) in the same expression — they are resolved at different times.

